WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.876 --> 00:00:09.047
Seems like only yesterday
my mother said to me,

00:00:09.047 --> 00:00:11.675
"The ugliest thing in the world

00:00:11.716 --> 00:00:13.802
is a naked man with socks on."

00:00:13.802 --> 00:00:17.847
(Laughter)

00:00:17.847 --> 00:00:21.977
Can you believe that was the first piece
of sex advice I ever received?

00:00:22.018 --> 00:00:23.478
(Laughter)

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:26.731
I was 11 years old, growing up in Kenya,

00:00:26.773 --> 00:00:30.819
and I believe this might have been
my mother's way of trying to scare me

00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:33.321
out of having intimate
relationships with men.

00:00:34.239 --> 00:00:35.407
It didn't.

00:00:35.448 --> 00:00:36.449
(Laughter)

00:00:36.491 --> 00:00:40.078
Instead, I became fascinated by sex.

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:43.331
I wanted to hear
other people's stories about sex

00:00:43.373 --> 00:00:47.210
and watch all the movies
with all the sex scenes.

00:00:47.544 --> 00:00:52.716
Everything about this very taboo subject
was so intriguing to me.

00:00:53.133 --> 00:00:54.801
Well, now my mum's gone.

00:00:55.218 --> 00:00:57.095
Nine years this year.

00:00:57.137 --> 00:00:59.389
And true to her word,

00:00:59.431 --> 00:01:02.350
the ugliest thing in the world
is a naked man with socks on.

00:01:02.392 --> 00:01:04.894
(Laughter)

00:01:05.270 --> 00:01:09.399
But over time, I have found things
to be far much uglier.

00:01:09.858 --> 00:01:12.402
It took me a ton of therapy

00:01:12.402 --> 00:01:17.991
to realize that my fixation with sex
was due to a traumatized childhood.

00:01:19.367 --> 00:01:23.330
See, I was sexually assaulted
when I was eight years old.

00:01:24.247 --> 00:01:26.416
And I never told anybody,

00:01:26.458 --> 00:01:30.003
because even in my
comedic-sex-advice household,

00:01:30.045 --> 00:01:32.380
I still didn't learn about consent.

00:01:32.422 --> 00:01:33.757
And I was afraid.

00:01:34.799 --> 00:01:36.676
Afraid that I would get into trouble.

00:01:37.427 --> 00:01:41.139
Afraid that it was my fault
or that nobody would believe me.

00:01:41.931 --> 00:01:43.600
Or, worse still,

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:46.519
afraid that my parents
would ground me forever.

00:01:47.145 --> 00:01:48.396
And I'm not alone.

00:01:49.230 --> 00:01:54.152
Men sexually assault women and girls
on a massive rate in Kenya,

00:01:54.194 --> 00:01:59.616
where 45 percent of women
aged between 15 and 49

00:01:59.616 --> 00:02:03.203
have reported either physical
or sexual violence.

00:02:03.244 --> 00:02:07.874
Actually, only 14 percent
have reported sexual violence.

00:02:08.291 --> 00:02:11.628
And this is possibly
because most of this violence

00:02:11.670 --> 00:02:14.506
happens in domestic partnerships,

00:02:14.547 --> 00:02:18.009
where the perpetrator
is known by the victim.

00:02:18.718 --> 00:02:22.472
And these patterns play out
all around the world.

00:02:23.139 --> 00:02:24.974
And I truly believe

00:02:24.974 --> 00:02:28.269
that it's a lack
of sex education in schools

00:02:28.269 --> 00:02:30.063
that is partially to blame.

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:32.190
Back home,

00:02:32.190 --> 00:02:37.821
the education system is one
of destroying your relationship with self,

00:02:37.862 --> 00:02:40.198
shaming you for your discovery

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:43.034
and then praising you
for how much you conform.

00:02:43.743 --> 00:02:48.998
This, coupled with disturbing
imagery of ailing genitals,

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:51.710
is aimed at teaching us one thing:

00:02:52.460 --> 00:02:55.797
to abstain from all sexual activity.

00:02:56.673 --> 00:03:00.009
The perfect puritanical society.

00:03:01.302 --> 00:03:03.805
But of course, young people
are still having sex.

00:03:04.681 --> 00:03:07.100
They just don't understand
the consequences

00:03:07.142 --> 00:03:08.977
of their adult-like choices.

00:03:09.769 --> 00:03:11.730
This, too, was my experience.

00:03:12.605 --> 00:03:14.774
I had zero resources growing up

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:20.363
and, unfortunately, often found myself
in less-than-favorable situations

00:03:20.405 --> 00:03:22.407
as a teen and a young adult.

00:03:24.576 --> 00:03:30.165
Add on to that coming out as a queer woman
in a very homophobic country.

00:03:31.666 --> 00:03:35.211
My therapist once jokingly said
that I needed to pick a struggle.

00:03:35.670 --> 00:03:39.758
(Laughter)

00:03:40.091 --> 00:03:41.760
All of this is to say,

00:03:41.801 --> 00:03:48.141
I really want to create a better
transition process for young people,

00:03:48.141 --> 00:03:52.562
because I truly believe
that the more we talk about sex,

00:03:52.604 --> 00:03:55.648
the safer and the better
it'll be for everybody.

00:03:56.232 --> 00:04:01.821
(Applause)

00:04:01.863 --> 00:04:03.490
So in 2016,

00:04:03.490 --> 00:04:08.787
I started a sex-positive podcast
called "The Spread."

00:04:09.370 --> 00:04:10.663
(Laughter)

00:04:10.705 --> 00:04:13.541
Targeted at a pan-African audience.

00:04:14.542 --> 00:04:16.920
I really wanted to create a safe space

00:04:16.961 --> 00:04:21.508
where young people could openly talk
about different aspects of their sexuality

00:04:21.549 --> 00:04:25.011
without feelings of shame or judgment.

00:04:25.970 --> 00:04:29.933
And it turns out
people love to talk about sex.

00:04:29.933 --> 00:04:31.100
(Laughter)

00:04:31.768 --> 00:04:33.728
And I've had the great pleasure and honor

00:04:33.770 --> 00:04:37.857
of answering a myriad of these questions
about sex on my podcast,

00:04:37.899 --> 00:04:40.360
such as, "My boyfriend says

00:04:40.401 --> 00:04:43.822
that if we have sex and it's my first time
and without a condom,

00:04:43.863 --> 00:04:45.323
that I won't get pregnant.

00:04:45.365 --> 00:04:46.491
Is this true?"

00:04:47.075 --> 00:04:48.535
Of course it's not true.

00:04:48.993 --> 00:04:53.122
Having sex without a condom poses
great risk of not only getting pregnant

00:04:53.122 --> 00:04:54.874
but contracting STIs.

00:04:55.291 --> 00:04:57.210
Or, “I watch too much porn,

00:04:57.252 --> 00:04:59.295
and I'm no longer aroused by my partner.

00:04:59.337 --> 00:05:00.839
Am I broken?"

00:05:01.631 --> 00:05:03.299
No, you're not broken.

00:05:03.842 --> 00:05:07.428
But too much porn can desensitize you
from real-life pleasures.

00:05:08.054 --> 00:05:10.598
Or, "I'm 24 years old

00:05:10.640 --> 00:05:13.643
and my friends make fun of me
because I'm a virgin.

00:05:13.685 --> 00:05:17.438
Should I have sex
just to gain popularity?"

00:05:17.438 --> 00:05:18.815
Absolutely not.

00:05:19.649 --> 00:05:22.151
First of all, virginity
is a social construct.

00:05:23.152 --> 00:05:26.322
And I think you should have
your sexual debut --

00:05:26.364 --> 00:05:27.532
(Applause)

00:05:27.574 --> 00:05:28.741
thank you --

00:05:28.783 --> 00:05:30.827
when you’re good and ready to.

00:05:30.869 --> 00:05:35.456
A lot of the time, we have a lot of fun
on the podcast, honestly.

00:05:35.498 --> 00:05:38.877
But sometimes it does get
a little bit serious,

00:05:38.877 --> 00:05:41.713
especially when it comes
to one topic in particular:

00:05:42.672 --> 00:05:44.173
consent.

00:05:44.215 --> 00:05:46.551
These are some of the questions I receive.

00:05:46.593 --> 00:05:50.471
"My husband insists on having sex with me
even when I don't want to.

00:05:50.513 --> 00:05:52.223
I've relayed my concerns.

00:05:52.223 --> 00:05:54.017
He always responds with,

00:05:54.017 --> 00:05:56.561
'You're my wife.
It's your place to do so.'

00:05:56.561 --> 00:05:58.521
How do I prevent this from happening?"

00:05:58.563 --> 00:06:01.524
Or, "I went out last night
and woke up this morning

00:06:01.524 --> 00:06:03.610
next to the guy that was chatting me up.

00:06:03.651 --> 00:06:06.738
I have no idea what happened,
but I think we had sex.

00:06:06.738 --> 00:06:08.197
What should I do?"

00:06:08.823 --> 00:06:10.575
It's conversations like these

00:06:10.617 --> 00:06:15.038
that reinforce the fact
that people don't have the first clue

00:06:15.079 --> 00:06:16.706
how to talk about consent.

00:06:17.498 --> 00:06:19.834
So it's become my life's work

00:06:19.834 --> 00:06:24.839
to create a curriculum
to educate young people on consent.

00:06:25.256 --> 00:06:28.760
Now the inspiration for this
might surprise you,

00:06:28.760 --> 00:06:32.138
but I got it in my 30s

00:06:32.180 --> 00:06:35.391
after a visit to a BDSM dungeon.

00:06:35.683 --> 00:06:37.352
(Laughter)

00:06:37.352 --> 00:06:38.978
For those of you that don't know,

00:06:39.020 --> 00:06:44.150
BDSM is a series of practices
and erotic role play

00:06:44.192 --> 00:06:48.154
that involve bondage, discipline,

00:06:48.154 --> 00:06:51.199
dominance and submission
and sadomasochism.

00:06:51.991 --> 00:06:54.994
Now I know, a lot of people
have a lot of misleading information

00:06:55.036 --> 00:06:57.038
about the BDSM community,

00:06:57.038 --> 00:06:58.665
but more often than not,

00:06:58.665 --> 00:07:02.210
we create and curate safe spaces

00:07:02.210 --> 00:07:06.798
with an array of toys and items
for the kinky community to play with,

00:07:06.798 --> 00:07:08.257
if they so please.

00:07:08.758 --> 00:07:10.218
It's like a playground.

00:07:10.843 --> 00:07:12.011
For adults.

00:07:12.011 --> 00:07:13.179
(Laughter)

00:07:13.846 --> 00:07:17.934
In BDSM, everything is negotiated
before it happens.

00:07:18.559 --> 00:07:20.770
And these are some
of the rules and regulations

00:07:20.812 --> 00:07:22.939
that would greet you upon entry.

00:07:23.815 --> 00:07:25.149
One:

00:07:25.191 --> 00:07:28.152
Do not touch anyone without asking.

00:07:28.528 --> 00:07:29.696
Even a hug,

00:07:29.696 --> 00:07:32.657
if you don't know somebody,
is a bad move without permission.

00:07:33.616 --> 00:07:34.742
Two:

00:07:34.784 --> 00:07:37.704
Do not touch anyone's toys
without permission.

00:07:38.162 --> 00:07:41.374
If you're not sure
if something is a toy, ask.

00:07:42.250 --> 00:07:43.459
Three:

00:07:43.501 --> 00:07:47.964
Consent can be withdrawn
at any time during an activity.

00:07:49.090 --> 00:07:50.842
And my personal favorite:

00:07:50.883 --> 00:07:53.177
if consent is not given,

00:07:53.219 --> 00:07:55.304
do not ask again.

00:07:55.638 --> 00:07:58.057
Accept and respect a "no,"

00:07:58.099 --> 00:08:00.435
as graciously as you would a "yes."

00:08:00.476 --> 00:08:05.523
(Applause)

00:08:06.107 --> 00:08:10.361
Now, in no way am I interested
in teaching children BDSM.

00:08:10.403 --> 00:08:11.529
(Laughter)

00:08:12.488 --> 00:08:17.827
But BDSM, a community
that is created strictly for adults

00:08:17.869 --> 00:08:20.955
that people view
as shameful and dangerous,

00:08:20.997 --> 00:08:23.958
has better guidelines
for learning about consent

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:26.419
than many homes or schools

00:08:26.419 --> 00:08:28.379
in many parts of the world.

00:08:28.796 --> 00:08:32.383
And like you've heard,
these rules aren't specifically sexual,

00:08:32.425 --> 00:08:34.510
but they can apply to sex.

00:08:35.303 --> 00:08:38.181
I truly think that the strategy

00:08:38.181 --> 00:08:41.768
to raising adults
with healthy sexual behaviors

00:08:41.809 --> 00:08:44.771
is to first teach kids about consent,

00:08:44.812 --> 00:08:46.147
like, super early,

00:08:46.147 --> 00:08:49.233
way before sex is even a topic
of conversation.

00:08:50.109 --> 00:08:52.570
Can you imagine
having conversations with kids

00:08:52.612 --> 00:08:57.075
and letting them know that everything
about their bodies can be negotiated?

00:08:57.075 --> 00:08:58.242
For example,

00:08:58.284 --> 00:09:02.038
let them decide who they want
to help them during bath time.

00:09:02.622 --> 00:09:03.998
Or tell them

00:09:04.040 --> 00:09:07.293
that they don't have to accept
that kiss on the cheek from grandma.

00:09:07.835 --> 00:09:10.463
Or tell them that they
have to ask for a permission

00:09:10.463 --> 00:09:12.715
before they play
with somebody else's toy truck.

00:09:13.674 --> 00:09:15.426
And let them know that they can say,

00:09:15.468 --> 00:09:18.137
"Actually my pronouns are they/them,"

00:09:18.137 --> 00:09:19.430
without feeling guilty.

00:09:19.472 --> 00:09:23.434
(Applause)

00:09:23.434 --> 00:09:27.480
It's these tools that will help
keep our children safe

00:09:27.522 --> 00:09:30.525
and respect people throughout their lives.

00:09:30.900 --> 00:09:34.112
We have the power to shape the future.

00:09:34.654 --> 00:09:36.531
The solutions are simple.

00:09:37.532 --> 00:09:39.867
It's the patriarchy
that's so damn difficult.

00:09:39.867 --> 00:09:41.494
(Laughter)

00:09:42.036 --> 00:09:46.207
(Applause)

00:09:46.249 --> 00:09:52.505
So let's engage five,
six or eight-year-olds

00:09:52.505 --> 00:09:55.258
on conversation around consent

00:09:55.299 --> 00:09:57.301
and bodily autonomy

00:09:57.343 --> 00:10:01.722
as a function of affirming their humanity,

00:10:01.764 --> 00:10:06.727
which in turn can look like adults
having safe, healthy,

00:10:06.769 --> 00:10:09.522
pleasurable and fun sex.

00:10:10.398 --> 00:10:14.235
Because consent isn't just about sex.

00:10:15.069 --> 00:10:19.157
It's first about communication
and relationships.

00:10:20.116 --> 00:10:21.284
Thank you.

00:10:21.325 --> 00:10:28.291
(Applause)

